        "committer": {
          "name": "Minh",
          "email": "mdiep@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-10-19 15:10:21.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20980 lnet: clamp net show min_dump_alloc to its type",
        "message": "LU-20980 lnet: clamp net show min_dump_alloc to its type\n\nLU-20221 sums the per-NI dump sizes straight into\ncb->min_dump_alloc, which is a u16 on older kernels. At ~6.5KB per\nNI, 0@lo plus 8 tcp NIs gives 66306, which wraps to 770 - smaller\nthan the U16_MAX it replaced. lnet_net_size_skb() also reloads\nprev_type from its LNET_NET_ANY argument, charging a key table for\nevery net, and the malformed-request exit in lnet_net_show_start()\nreturns without freeing nlist.\n\nSum into a local ssize_t and cap at the field's maximum, keeping\nlarge nodes at the pre-LU-20221 size rather than failing. Track\nprev_type from the net being sized, and take the malformed-request\nexit through report_err.\n\nTLC-bugid: TLU-301\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-lnet env=ONLY=113\nFixes: 6fab1fe4a5c5 (\"LU-9680 lnet: handle multi-rail setups\")\nSigned-off-by: Minh Diep <mdiep@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Iafec3a7b21a266b5f4e93375b587337a91eae687\nAssisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master",
      "description": "Edit commit message"
    }
